            <h1>Build a Map-Based Property Explorer with SuperControl and Leaflet</h1>
            <p class="lead">Build a holiday-rental search experience where the result list, map, dates, guests and URL stay in sync, using SuperControl data, OpenStreetMap tiles and Leaflet.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="sv-doc">
            <h2>What you are building</h2>
            <p>The finished page is available at <a class="text-link" href="/supercontrol-property-explorer">/supercontrol-property-explorer</a>. It includes:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>a result list and map that respond to the same search state;</li>
                <li>search within the visible map area;</li>
                <li>marker clustering and spiderfying for dense groups;</li>
                <li>date, guest and location filters;</li>
                <li>property and location suggestions;</li>
                <li>mobile list and map views;</li>
                <li>stable URLs that can be bookmarked or shared;</li>
                <li>a hand-off to the existing property and booking journey.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The interaction model is familiar to users of large holiday-rental sites, but the layout, copy, markup and styling are original to this project.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="sv-doc">
            <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>.NET 10 SDK</li>
                <li>a SuperControl API token and account ID</li>
                <li>the existing <code>ISuperControlClient</code> connection from the listing-site demo</li>
                <li>Leaflet 1.9.4 and Leaflet.markercluster 1.5.3</li>
            </ul>
            <pre class="sc-pre">dotnet restore supercontrol-listing-site-demo-public.sln
dotnet run --project supercontrol-listing-site-demo.csproj</pre>
        </section>

        <section class="sv-doc">
            <h2>Core files</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><code>Controllers/PropertyExplorerController.cs</code></li>
                <li><code>Features/PropertyExplorer/PropertyExplorerViewModelFactory.cs</code></li>
                <li><code>ViewModels/PropertyExplorer/PropertyExplorerRequestViewModel.cs</code></li>
                <li><code>ViewModels/PropertyExplorer/PropertyExplorerResponseViewModel.cs</code></li>
                <li><code>Integrations/SuperControl/SuperControlListingSiteService.cs</code></li>
